 tax code to recognize it  and so of a company invest money in a  machine the tax code lets them keep that  money but if families are raising  children the tax code doesn't take that  into account so I'm just trying to  create equality between companies and  people and she's been very supportive of  that concept so I do think that she is  someone who has gotten the president in  the White House to care about that issue  because it's not something he campaigned  on and so she's been an important ally  in that fight and what's the view of the  American Society of the fact that  President Trump brought some members of  his family into the White House well  it's something we haven't seen since the  Kennedy administration but by and large  I don't think that there were a country  with some diverse opinions I think the  public opinion polls in the last  election reflected that were pretty  evenly divided between those that have  supported the president and those that  did not it was a very close election and  he ultimately won and I would say that  of the people that have problems  President Trump that's probably the  lowest item on their list there are a  lot of other things that they opposed  and as far as the role that they've  played his family members being his  son-in-law and his daughter as I said  his daughters had a very productive role  and his son-in-law seems to have  generally as well so I would say that  even for opponents of President Trump  the presence of Jared and Ivanka in the  administration is probably the least of  their complaints given some of the other  things that they have problems with my  last question it's a personal question  because you introduced a legislation to  designate the block in front of the  Russian embassy as Boris Nemtsov Plaza  in honor of my father why do you think  it is important yes two things one I  hope that soon  you've sooner rather than later there  will be a new Russian government that  will be proud that that name is on the  street not offended by it and the second  is that this is an issue that an  investigation that deserves an answer  we've seen individuals that were  convicted  whether it was them or not what about  why it happened who did it is one thing  why they did it is another this is a  political assassination this was a  prominent person in government that for  many years have been a part of  government who had a difference of  opinion with the direction that the  country was headed under Vladimir Putin  and it cost him his life and not only do  what we never know as long as Putin is  in power but they almost looked like it  doesn't matter and I think that that  that speaks not simply to the gloss of  the nation but to its soul and to what  does it mean to a society when you're  telling them that political opponents  it's okay to kill them because it what  does that do to a country into its  future into its collective soul as a  nation into its identity so this goes  well beyond simply one murder it goes to  be it speaks volumes to the future of a  society that that has some important  decisions to make here over the next  decade so thank you very much thank you
 

